<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>CYBS 4305 - Lecture 03: Security Risk Analysis & Methodologies</title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&family=Share+Tech+Mono&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <style>
        /* BASE CSS VARIABLES */
        :root {
            --bg-color: #080b12;
            --surface-color: #121824;
            --surface-accent: #1e293b;
            --text-primary: #f8fafc;
            --text-secondary: #94a3b8;
            --accent-primary: #38bdf8;
            --accent-glow: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.5);
            --highlight-yellow: #facc15;
            --highlight-green: #4ade80;
            --highlight-purple: #c084fc;
            --correct-color: #22c55e;
            --wrong-color: #ef4444;
            --border-radius: 12px;
            --font-main: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
            --card-border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3);
        }

        /* 8 HIGH-CONTRAST THEMES */
        body.theme-cyberpunk {
            --bg-color: #0a0118; --surface-color: #160233; --surface-accent: #280454;
            --text-primary: #ffffff; --text-secondary: #d8b4fe;
            --accent-primary: #f06292; --accent-glow: rgba(240, 98, 146, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #ffd54f; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(240, 98, 146, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-matrix {
            --bg-color: #020a02; --surface-color: #051a05; --surface-accent: #0a2e0a;
            --text-primary: #e8ffe8; --text-secondary: #86efac;
            --accent-primary: #22c55e; --accent-glow: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --font-main: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;
            --card-border: 1px solid rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-synthwave {
            --bg-color: #110826; --surface-color: #210d47; --surface-accent: #37146e;
            --text-primary: #ffffff; --text-secondary: #f472b6;
            --accent-primary: #fb923c; --accent-glow: rgba(251, 146, 60, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(251, 146, 60, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-deepsea {
            --bg-color: #031321; --surface-color: #0a2540; --surface-accent: #11385f;
            --text-primary: #f0f9ff; --text-secondary: #7dd3fc;
            --accent-primary: #06b6d4; --accent-glow: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-emerald {
            --bg-color: #022c22; --surface-color: #064e3b; --surface-accent: #047857;
            --text-primary: #ecfdf5; --text-secondary: #6ee7b7;
            --accent-primary: #10b981; --accent-glow: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-crimson {
            --bg-color: #1a0505; --surface-color: #3b0707; --surface-accent: #5c0a0a;
            --text-primary: #fff5f5; --text-secondary: #fca5a5;
            --accent-primary: #f87171; --accent-glow: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.4);
        }
        body.theme-violet {
            --bg-color: #120324; --surface-color: #240647; --surface-accent: #3b0a70;
            --text-primary: #faf5ff; --text-secondary: #c084fc;
            --accent-primary: #a855f7; --accent-glow: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.6);
            --highlight-yellow: #fef08a; --card-border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4);
        }

        /* GLOBAL RESET & STYLES */
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: var(--font-main);
            transition: background-color 0.8s ease, color 0.4s ease, border-color 0.5s ease;
        }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg-color); color: var(--text-primary);
            overflow-x: hidden; line-height: 1.6;
        }

        /* CANVAS BACKGROUND */
        #bg-canvas {
            position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100vw; height: 100vh;
            z-index: -1; opacity: 0.55; pointer-events: none;
        }

        /* HUD BAR & THEME CONTROL */
        #hud {
            position: sticky; top: 0; background: rgba(8, 11, 18, 0.88);
            backdrop-filter: blur(12px); padding: 12px 25px; display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; z-index: 100;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-primary); box-shadow: 0 0 25px var(--accent-glow);
            flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px;
        }

        .hud-group { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }

        .hud-stat {
            display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06); padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: var(--border-radius);
            border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary); text-shadow: 0 0 5px var(--accent-glow);
        }

        /* THEME TIMER CONTROLS */
        .theme-ctrl-btn {
            background: var(--accent-primary); color: #000; border: none;
            width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: bold; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
        }
        .theme-ctrl-btn:hover { transform: scale(1.15); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--accent-glow); }

        .timer-bar-container { width: 110px; background: #1e293b; border-radius: 6px; height: 8px; overflow: hidden; position: relative; }
        .timer-bar-fill { height: 100%; width: 100%; background: var(--accent-primary); transition: width 1s linear; }

        /* AUDIO PLAYER (FLOATING) */
        #audio-player {
            position: fixed; bottom: 20px; left: 20px; z-index: 100;
            background: var(--surface-color); padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: var(--border-radius);
            border: 2px solid var(--accent-primary); display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
        }

        .audio-btn {
            background: var(--accent-primary); color: #000; border: none;
            width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 50%; cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 1.1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            transition: transform 0.2s;
        }
        .audio-btn:hover { transform: scale(1.1); }
        input[type="range"] { accent-color: var(--accent-primary); cursor: pointer; }

        /* MAIN CONTAINER */
        .container { max-width: 1200px; margin: 30px auto; padding: 0 20px; }

        /* HEADER */
        header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 45px; }
        header h1 {
            font-size: 2.6rem; color: var(--accent-primary); text-shadow: 0 0 20px var(--accent-glow);
            text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        header .subtitle { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 500; }
        header .univ-tag { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--accent-primary); opacity: 0.9; margin-top: 5px; }

        /* SECTION HEADERS */
        h2.section-title {
            font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 40px 0 20px 0; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--accent-primary);
            padding-bottom: 8px; display: inline-block; text-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--accent-glow);
        }

        /* CARDS & HIGHLIGHTS */
        .card {
            background: var(--surface-color); padding: 25px 30px; border-radius: var(--border-radius);
            margin-bottom: 25px; border: var(--card-border); box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
            position: relative;
        }

        .highlight-def {
            background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);
            padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 1.05rem;
        }

        .badge-tag {
            display: inline-block; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 12px; font-size: 0.82rem;
            font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-right: 6px;
        }
        .badge-quant { background: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.2); color: #4ade80; border: 1px solid #22c55e; }
        .badge-qual { background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid #a855f7; }
        .badge-alert { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2); color: #f87171; border: 1px solid #ef4444; }

        .term-key { color: var(--highlight-yellow); font-weight: 700; }

        .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 25px; }
        .grid-3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }

        /* FLIP CARDS */
        .flip-card { height: 210px; perspective: 1000px; cursor: pointer; }
        .flip-card-inner { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%; text-align: center; transition: transform 0.6s; transform-style: preserve-3d; }
        .flip-card:hover .flip-card-inner { transform: rotateY(180deg); }
        .flip-card-front, .flip-card-back {
            position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 100%; backface-visibility: hidden;
            display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            padding: 20px; border-radius: var(--border-radius); background: var(--surface-color);
            border: var(--card-border);
        }
        .flip-card-front { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-primary); }
        .flip-card-back { transform: rotateY(180deg); font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); background: var(--surface-accent); }

        /* FORMULAS & CALCULATOR */
        .formula-box {
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border: 2px dashed var(--accent-primary); padding: 20px;
            border-radius: var(--border-radius); text-align: center; margin: 15px 0;
        }
        .formula-box h3 { font-family: monospace; font-size: 2rem; color: var(--accent-primary); text-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--accent-glow); }

        .calc-input { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
        input[type="number"] {
            padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary);
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5); color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; outline: none;
        }
        input[type="number"]:focus { box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--accent-glow); }

        .btn-action {
            padding: 12px 24px; background: var(--accent-primary); color: #000; border: none;
            border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem;
            text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; transition: all 0.2s;
        }
        .btn-action:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 8px 20px var(--accent-glow); filter: brightness(1.1); }

        .calc-result-box {
            font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 15px; color: #000;
            background: var(--accent-primary); padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;
        }

        /* TABLES */
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; border-radius: var(--border-radius); overflow: hidden; }
        th, td { border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); padding: 12px 15px; text-align: left; }
        th { background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2); color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1.05rem; }
        tr:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); }

        /* QUIZ */
        .quiz-option {
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); padding: 15px 20px; border-radius: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 12px; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
            transition: all 0.2s; font-size: 1.05rem;
        }
        .quiz-option:hover { border-color: var(--accent-primary); background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1); transform: translateX(5px); }
        .quiz-option.correct { background: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.25); border-color: var(--correct-color); color: #4ade80; font-weight: 700; }
        .quiz-option.wrong { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25); border-color: var(--wrong-color); color: #f87171; }

        .quiz-feedback {
            display: none; padding: 15px; margin-top: 12px; border-radius: 8px;
            background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1rem;
        }

        /* FLASH EFFECT ON THEME CHANGE */
        .flash-overlay { position: fixed; top:0; left:0; width:100vw; height:100vh; background: white; z-index:9999; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.4s; }
        .flash-active { opacity: 0.2 !important; }

        @media (max-width: 850px) {
            .grid-2, .grid-3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            header h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
            #hud { justify-content: center; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="theme-cyberpunk" onload="initApp()">

    <div class="flash-overlay" id="flash"></div>
    <canvas id="bg-canvas"></canvas>

    <!-- HUD BAR -->
    <div id="hud">
        <!-- THEME TIMER & CONTROLS -->
        <div class="hud-group">
            <div class="hud-stat">
                <i class="fas fa-palette"></i> Vibe Shift:
                <button class="theme-ctrl-btn" onclick="prevTheme()" title="Previous Theme"><i class="fas fa-chevron-left"></i></button>
                <button class="theme-ctrl-btn" id="timer-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleTimer()" title="Pause/Play Theme Timer"><i class="fas fa-pause"></i></button>
                <button class="theme-ctrl-btn" onclick="nextTheme()" title="Next Theme"><i class="fas fa-chevron-right"></i></button>
                <div class="timer-bar-container"><div class="timer-bar-fill" id="timer-fill"></div></div>
                <span id="time-left" style="width: 24px; text-align: center;">30</span>s
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hud-group">
            <div class="hud-stat"><i class="fas fa-fire" style="color:#f97316;"></i> Streak: <span id="streak">1</span> Day</div>
            <div class="hud-stat"><i class="fas fa-trophy" style="color:#facc15;"></i> Level: <span id="level">1</span></div>
            <div class="hud-stat"><i class="fas fa-bolt" style="color:#38bdf8;"></i> XP: <span id="xp-counter">0</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- AUDIO PLAYER (FLOATING) -->
    <div id="audio-player">
        <button class="audio-btn" id="play-btn" onclick="toggleAudio()"><i class="fas fa-play"></i></button>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:2px;">
            <span style="font-size:0.8rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent-primary);">LO-FI STUDY BEATS</span>
            <input type="range" id="vol-slider" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.3" onchange="changeVolume()">
        </div>
        <audio id="bg-music" loop>
            <source src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/download/audio/2022/05/27/audio_1808fbf07a.mp3?filename=lofi-study-112191.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
        </audio>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- HEADER -->
        <header>
            <h1>CYBS 4305: Security Risk Analysis</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Lecture 03: Cyber Risk Assessment and Analysis Methodologies</div>
            <div class="univ-tag">University of Hafr Al Batin | College of Computer Science and Engineering</div>
        </header>

        <!-- SECTION 1: WHAT IS SRA & GOALS -->
        <h2 class="section-title">1. Introduction to Security Risk Assessment</h2>
        <div class="card" onclick="addXP(10)">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-shield-halved" style="color:var(--accent-primary);"></i> What is Security Risk Assessment?</h3>
            <div class="highlight-def">
                <strong>Official Definition:</strong> An <span class="term-key">objective analysis</span> of the effectiveness of the current security controls that protect an organization's assets and a determination of the <span class="term-key">probability of losses</span> to those assets.
            </div>
            <div class="highlight-def">
                <strong>The Ultimate Goal:</strong> To understand and measure security risks to information assets, enabling the organization to make <span class="term-key">informed decisions</span> to mitigate those risks and preserve its mission.
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> A complete assessment evaluates <span class="term-key">Assets, Threats, Vulnerabilities, Existing Controls, Likelihood, and Impact</span> to prioritize security improvements according to organizational risk.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2: SECURITY DRIVERS -->
        <h2 class="section-title">2. Why is Risk Assessment a Priority? (Security Drivers)</h2>
        <div class="card grid-2" onclick="addXP(15)">
            <div>
                <h3><i class="fas fa-compass" style="color:var(--accent-primary);"></i> Security Drivers Comparison</h3>
                <p>Organizations are driven by several factors to implement security. However, a <span class="term-key">Risk-Driven</span> approach provides the most comprehensive strategy.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span class="badge-tag badge-alert">Audit-Driven</span>
                        <strong>Reactive:</strong> Focuses strictly on what is already known and documented.
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span class="badge-tag badge-qual">Technology-Driven</span>
                        <strong>Can lead to gaps:</strong> Ignores administrative & physical controls.
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span class="badge-tag badge-qual">Compliance-Driven</span>
                        <strong>Creates silos:</strong> Meets standards (e.g., HIPAA, PCI DSS) but lacks broad implementation guidance.
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span class="badge-tag badge-quant">Risk-Driven</span>
                        <strong>Most Complete:</strong> Addresses risk to organizational assets as the primary concern.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3: KEY TERMINOLOGY & EQUATION -->
        <h2 class="section-title">3. Key Terminology & The Risk Equation</h2>
        <p style="text-align: center; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 15px;">(Hover or tap cards to flip and test your memory)</p>
        <div class="grid-3">
            <div class="flip-card" onclick="addXP(5)">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                    <div class="flip-card-front"><i class="fas fa-database" style="font-size:2.2rem; margin-bottom:10px;"></i> Asset</div>
                    <div class="flip-card-back">Any resource, data, or item of value to the organization (<span class="term-key">tangible or intangible</span>).</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card" onclick="addXP(5)">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                    <div class="flip-card-front"><i class="fas fa-user-ninja" style="font-size:2.2rem; margin-bottom:10px;"></i> Threat Agent</div>
                    <div class="flip-card-back">The entity that may cause a threat to happen (e.g., <span class="term-key">nature, malicious hackers, employees</span>).</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card" onclick="addXP(5)">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                    <div class="flip-card-front"><i class="fas fa-bug" style="font-size:2.2rem; margin-bottom:10px;"></i> Vulnerability</div>
                    <div class="flip-card-back">A <span class="term-key">flaw or oversight</span> in an existing control that may allow a threat agent to exploit it.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flip-card" onclick="addXP(5)">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                    <div class="flip-card-front"><i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation" style="font-size:2.2rem; margin-bottom:10px;"></i> Security Risk</div>
                    <div class="flip-card-back">The <span class="term-key">loss potential</span> to an asset that will likely occur if a threat exploits a vulnerability.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-box" onclick="addXP(10)">
            <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 5px;">The Conceptual Core Formula:</p>
            <h3>Risk = Assets × Threat × Vulnerability</h3>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.95rem;">Risk combines asset value, threat frequency, and vulnerability likelihood. Goal: Reduce likelihood, impact, or both.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4: MANAGEMENT PROCESS CYCLE -->
        <h2 class="section-title">4. The Security Risk Management Cycle</h2>
        <div class="card grid-2" onclick="addXP(15)">
            <div>
                <h3><i class="fas fa-rotate" style="color:var(--accent-primary);"></i> The 4-Stage Continuous Cycle</h3>
                <p>Security Risk Assessment is one part of an ongoing operational cycle:</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <ol style="margin-left: 20px; line-height: 1.9;">
                    <li><strong>Risk Assessment:</strong> Analyze threats, vulnerabilities, asset impacts, and countermeasures.</li>
                    <li><strong>Test and Review:</strong> Examination of controls against requirements (e.g., <span class="term-key">vulnerability scanning, audit of controls</span>).</li>
                    <li><strong>Risk Mitigation:</strong> Reducing risk by implementing safeguards and additional controls.</li>
                    <li><strong>Operational Security:</strong> Day-to-day security operations (<span class="term-key">patches, incident handling, training</span>).</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 5: QUANTITATIVE VS QUALITATIVE -->
        <h2 class="section-title">5. Quantitative vs. Qualitative Analysis</h2>
        <div class="card grid-2">
            <div style="background: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.05); padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.3);">
                <h3><span class="badge-tag badge-quant">Quantitative</span> Analysis</h3>
                <p>Relies on specific formulas and calculations to determine security risk in <strong>dollar figures ($)</strong> (e.g., Annual Loss Expectancy).</p>
                <br>
                <p style="color: #4ade80;"><strong>Advantages:</strong></p>
                <ul style="margin-left:20px; font-size:0.95rem;">
                    <li><strong>Objective:</strong> Predetermined formulas reduce subjective bias.</li>
                    <li><strong>Real Numbers:</strong> Expressed in dollar values.</li>
                    <li><strong>Easily Understood:</strong> Simple clear math outcomes.</li>
                    <li><strong>Meaningful Statistics:</strong> Helps track changes over time.</li>
                    <li><strong>Credible:</strong> Statements like "$3.16 million loss" carry weight.</li>
                </ul>
                <br>
                <p style="color: #f87171;"><strong>Disadvantages:</strong></p>
                <ul style="margin-left:20px; font-size:0.95rem;">
                    <li><strong>Complex:</strong> Requires experienced project members.</li>
                    <li><strong>Labor-Intensive:</strong> Huge amount of data gathering.</li>
                    <li><strong style="color: #ef4444;">False Sense of Accuracy:</strong> (Biggest flaw!) Output looks exact, but input variables are often based on guesswork.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.05); padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);">
                <h3><span class="badge-tag badge-qual">Qualitative</span> Analysis</h3>
                <p>Relies on subjective judgment and descriptive terms like <strong>"High", "Medium", "Low"</strong> using lookup charts/tables.</p>
                <br>
                <p style="color: #4ade80;"><strong>Advantages:</strong></p>
                <ul style="margin-left:20px; font-size:0.95rem;">
                    <li><strong>Simple:</strong> Relief from quantitative complex data gathering.</li>
                    <li><strong>Simple Measurement:</strong> Easy for teams to agree an email server outage is a "Major Loss".</li>
                    <li><strong>Easy to Convey:</strong> Simple descriptive terms.</li>
                    <li><strong>Adequate Identification:</strong> Sufficient to prioritize security posture fixes.</li>
                </ul>
